{
 "standing": "The closing digest law of identity-and-evidence section 3, extended to this bundle. Every 64-hex or sha256: field here carries x-opensip-digest naming its representation, retention and authority. There is no default and no residue: a new field added without an annotation is inadmissible, exactly as in identity-schemas.v3.",
 "representations": [
  "raw-artifact",
  "canonical-record",
  "h-identity"
 ],
 "retention": {
  "preimage": "the exact preimage bytes are retained under this digest",
  "preimage-frame": "the retained object is the H preimage frame, so SHA256(retained bytes) is the digest",
  "closure-tree-member": "the digest must be a member digest of the retained signed closure tree the annotation names",
  "owner-retained": "the named owning contract retains and admits the bytes; this bundle joins by digest equality",
  "derived": "Recompute the identity from the retained owning record, with no separately retained preimage frame. In this bundle the three SourceUnitOwnershipV1 unitId positions resolve through units[]: derive H(native.compilation-unit.v1, UnitIdentityV1{schemaVersion:1, markerPath, targetKind, targetName}) from the matching row and compare; selectedUnitIds and ownership[].unitId must name a row in that same closed table."
 },
